DE02 (MUTATE=1) COMPLETE: 11/15 checks PASS -- the broken hinge FAILs as required.
THEOREM (certified): for the rule g = nu(sqrt(x^2+eta^2)) g_N, x = (r_M/r)^2, any C^1 kernel nu, any eta > 0:
  lim_{r->inf} v(r)^2 r = nu(eta) G M_b,  with  v^2 r = G M_b [nu(eta) + x^2 nu'(eta)/(2 eta) + O(x^4)]
  -- the floor is PARAMETER-FREE: fixed by the registered nu(eta) alone (no kernel derivative, no scale, no eta-gradient).
DE05 (decline shape): fitted |d ln v/d ln r + 0.5| <= 0.1 at r >= 10 r_M marks an EFE-type decline (framework 4.9e-01 to 6.9e-08, AQUAL 0.0 at 30 r_M); NFW (c=10) slopes at its measurable radii [-0.22, +0.27] fail that bar by >= 0.25 -- but with r_J = 1.8e-07 r_M the halo is only measurable inside r_J, where the EFE curves are still shallow: DE05 alone cannot separate the pair AQUAL/framework (|Delta slope| <= 4.9e-01 at 30 r_M).
DE06 (floor): decision bar = median over eta-grid of log10(floor ratio) must exceed 0.4 dex: framework/Newton 0.121-0.443 dex (always > 0); AQUAL/framework +0.068 dex at eta=0.5, sign flips near eta~1.45 (median |.| 0.092 -> NOT separable); NFW5/framework medians 0.404/0.428 > 0.4 -> SEPARATES (PASS);  NFW3 medians 0.182/0.206 < 0.4 -> does not separate (FAIL as registered).
